§ `22. search and seizure`

`search: information and reasonable cause` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS TRUE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS FALSE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS FALSE

`search: concealed and delay` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS TRUE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS TRUE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS FALSE

`search: concealed, no delay` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS TRUE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS FALSE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS FALSE

`search: delay, nothing concealed` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS TRUE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS FALSE

`search: warrant issued` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS FALSE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS TRUE

`search: nothing` MEANS `Search Facts` WITH
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS FALSE
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS FALSE
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS FALSE

